#passage-box(title: "MODEL EMAIL – ĐỀ SỐ 02, QUESTION 35 (134 words)")[
  Dear Alex,

  How is your new school semester going? In your last email, you asked how my family shares housework, so I'm glad to tell you about our daily routine.

  Because both of my parents work full-time, all four members divide household chores equally. My mother usually does the grocery shopping and cooks dinner, while my father does the laundry and handles the heavy lifting at weekends. As for my younger brother and me, we sweep the floor, wash the dishes after meals, and put out the rubbish every evening.

  In my opinion, sharing housework is truly important for teenagers. It teaches us valuable life skills, responsibility, and gratitude for our parents' hard work, and it brings everyone closer together. Which chores do you often do at home?

  Write back soon!

  Best wishes,\
  Nam
]

